smartinit.v3.2.4
Q3FY14 Downscaling Implementation

===================================================================================
1.  DGEX DOWN-SCALING (NET=DGEX, RUN=DGEX)
===================================================================================

1A. Additional SREF and DGEX post-processing

Additional jobs are needed to extend SREF GEFS look-alike files from 90-192 forecast hours.
This requires additional tasks for MPMD jobs described below

The following prep jobs are triggered once the GEFS 21 member sig files thru 192 forecast hours are available.
(by arount +2:30 hours after cycle time for 03,09,15,21 UTC SREF runs)
NOTE: These gefs2sref jobs will be run as part of the SREF system upgrade for smartinit downscaling.


All upgrades are also available on svn at https://svnemc.ncep.noaa.gov/projects/smartinit

ECF PREP JOB: 
=============
NOTE: SMVER= smartinit version number if running JSREF ecf/jobs from smartinit dir.
      SMVER set in jsref_gefs2sref.ecf or versions/smartinit.ver = v3.2.4
I.  /meso/save/Jeff.McQueen/smartinit.v3.2.4/ecf/jsref_gefs2sref.ecf     
(mpmd job,43 tasks, 3 hrly GEFS Fhrs 00-->126)
(NOTE: This should replace current operational ecf script in SREEF network)
Can be submitted once GEFS sig files are available thru 126 hours.

II.  /meso/save/Jeff.McQueen/smartinit.v3.2.4/ecf/jsref_gefs2sref132.ecf  
(mpmd job,11 tasks, 6 hrly GEFS Fhrs 132-->192)
Can be submitted once GEFS sig files are available thru 192 hours.

NOTE: One task is required for each GEFS forecast hour for this ECF MPMD script

The driving ecf script is further divided into two parts:

* One for all 3 hour GEFS forecast hours:  00 thru 126       (43 Tasks Used,~40 mins).
  and 
* One for all 6 hour GEFS forecast hours:  132 thru 192      (11 Tasks required, ~ 10 mins).
  This is because after 126 hours, GEFS sig outputs are only available every 6 hours.
NOTE: if changing the starting and ending forecast hours, you must change the number of tasks in 
the driving ecf script  BSUB cards to correspond to the number of forecast files to be processed.

 JOBS: 
========
    ../jobs/JSREF_WRFGFSPREP  ---> Create individual GEFS member files interpolated to SREF grids
    ../jobs/JSREF_GEFS2SREF   ---> Create SREF ensemble product files from interpolated GEFS members.
also
   ../jobs/JDGEX_NAM2DGEX  --> Interpolate NAM 78 hour native grid parent forecast files  
                            to DGEX Conus grid (185) for conus dgex downscaling.
  NOTE: this NAM2DGEX job will be implemented as part of the DGEX system upgrade

 SCRIPTS:
==========
    ../scripts/exsref_wrf_gfsprep.sh.ecf  (30 wall clock mins for 0-126 hrs)
    ../scripts/exsref_gefs2sref.sh.ecf    (3 wall clock mins for 0-126 hrs)
   ../scripts exsref_enspost4GEFS.sh.ecf  (3 wall clock mins for 0-126 hrs)
   /nwprod/sref.v6.1.1/ush/sref_prep_sig2pgb.sh  (not modified, in the SREF NETwork)

  SOURCE:
=========
 ../sorc/sref_ens_gen.fd

  PARM:
========
  ../parm/sref_para_config (To set local in, output dirs from parm file if desired)

These jobs and scripts perform the same tasks (with the same names) that are
currently run as part of the SREF system through 90 forecast hours 4x/day.


****INPUT****
-------------
  COMENS=/com/gens/prod/gefs.yyyymmdd/{CYC}
    /sfcsig/ge{GLBPAIR}.t{CYC}.sf{HHH}
    /sflux/ge{GLBPAIR}.t{CYC}.sfluxgrbf{HHH}
  where GLBPAIR=ctl,p1,p2....p20
  
 or 

 COMGFS=/com/gfs/prod/gfs.yyyymmdd/gfs.t{CYC}z.sf{HHHH} and .sfluxgrbf{HHH}


****OUTPUT is currently stored at COM_OUT=/ptmpp1/Jeff.McQueen/com/sref/para
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Intermediate GENS SIG member files converted to global pgrb format (and gfs master file)
   and reduced to contain only input needed for final product generation output 
... sref.yyyymmmdd/global_pgrb/
  gens_p{P##}.t{CYC}z.pgrbf{HHH} 
  gfs.t{CYC}z.master.grb{HHH}
where P##=ctl,1,2,3..20

2. Intermediate gens member predictions interpolated to SREF grids
... sref.yyyymmdd/{CYC}/pgrb_gefs/
  sref_{MDL}.t{CYC}z.pgrb{GRD}.p{P##}.f{HHH}
where MDL=nmm,nmb,em
      GRD=212,216 or 243

3. Final GENS product (mean, spread, prob) files on SREF GRIDSA
...  sref.yyyymmdd/ensprod_gefs/{CYC}
  sref.t{CYC}z.pgrb{GRD}.{prbtyp}_3hrly.grib (or grib2)
where
  prbtyp=mean,max,min,mod,spread,prob,p10,p25,p50,p75 or p90
  5 MB/file


========================================================================
1B.  JDGEX_SMINIT   --> downscale dgex step
=========================================================================
ECF additional dgex smartinit jobs: that are run every 3 hrs to 192 DGEX forecast hours 
NCO should run JDGEX_SMINIT every 3 forecast hours beginning with the DGEX start hour 
and ending at DGEX forecast hour 192.
The downscaling is run once the dgex bsmart files are available.  Otherwise, run as is done
for NAM smartinit ecflow processing.
In ecf dir:
  ~/smartinit.v3.2.4/ecf/jdgex_sminit_conus_fHH.ecf (HH=78,81...192)   CYCLE 06/18 UTC
  ~/smartinit.v3.2.4/ecf/jdgex_sminit_ak3_fHH.ecf (HH=84,93..192)      CYCLE 00/12 UTC

JOBS (/jobs):       JDGEX_SMINIT
SCRIPTS (/scripts): jdgex_smartinit.sh.ecf
USH (/ush):         jdgex_smartinit.sh

Additional parm  prdgen control files
  ../parm/dgex_masterak3.ctl
  ../parm/dgex_masterconus.ctl

Additional fix wgt prdgen files
 ../fix/wgt/dgex_wgt_184_conus   (interp to 2.5 km grid 184)
../fix/wgt/dgex_wgt_91_alaska    (interp to 3 km grid 91)
=============================================================================================

Once the jsref_gefs2sref.ecf ecf job is complete from the SREF Network, 
the smartinit system (JDGEX_SMINIT) can be run with: 

export RUNTYP=dgex_ak --->  for downscaling to Alaska 3 km grid at cycles 00/12 UTC  
(smartinit invoked from ECFlow every 3 hrs for forecast hours 84-->192)

export RUNTYP=dgex_cs --->  for downscaling to CONUS 2.5 km grid at cycles 06/18 UTC   
(smartinit invoked from ECFLOW every 3 hrs for forecast hours 78-->192)

INPUT: dgex bsmart files

OUTPUT: dgex.t{06/18}z.smartconus2p5{HHH}.tm00 (or grib2) from forecast hours 78 thru 192
90-130 MB per 3 hr forecast hour
5 wall clock mins/forecast hr

OUTPUT: dgex.t{00/12}z.smartak3{HHH}.tm00 (or grib2)      from forecast hours 84 thru 192
45-64 MB per 3 hr forecast hour
3 wall clock mins/forecast hr


